    "roles": ["band_member", "bandleader", "producer", "clinician", "percussionist"],
    "summary": "English drummer of Emerson, Lake & Palmer (1970-79, 1992-98) and Asia (1981-91, from 2006), earlier of the Crazy World of Arthur Brown and Atomic Rooster. Taught by the classical percussionist James Blades and raised on Morello, Philly Joe Jones, Blakey, Krupa and Rich, he played ELP's classical adaptations and odd meters with a big-band drummer's hands: Tarkus was written from a 10/8 rhythm he played on a practice pad. His 1973 kit was stainless steel. Modern Drummer Hall of Fame, 1989."
  },
